1
00:00:02,899 --> 00:00:05,510
Lesson three, Ted's day at school.

2
00:00:06,339 --> 00:00:09,810
Ted tells his parents he did poorly on his chemistry test.

3
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:13,189
They tell him he needs to get serious and study more.

4
00:00:14,519 --> 00:00:16,549
How was your day at school today, Ted?

5
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:17,349
Bad.

6
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:19,910
I had a chemistry test and I blew it.

7
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:23,329
Maybe if you didn't cut class so often, you'd do better.

8
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:24,389
That's right son.

9
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:26,750
Stop slacking off and start hitting the books.

10
00:00:27,179 --> 00:00:29,349
But I can't stand chemistry class.

11
00:00:29,199 --> 00:00:31,429
Besides, it's a lost cause.

12
00:00:31,899 --> 00:00:33,670
That class is way over my head.

13
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:35,750
You need to buckle down.

14
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:40,469
When I'm a famous musician, people won't give a hoot about my knowledge of atoms and

15
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:41,070
molecules.

16
00:00:41,479 --> 00:00:42,949
That's beside the point.

17
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:46,729
We know you have your heart set on going to New York University.

18
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:49,949
And you don't stand a chance of getting in there with such poor grades.

